6
00:00:14,599 --> 00:00:17,719
Scarcity written by survival.

7
00:00:17,839 --> 00:00:22,986
Among the 10,000 Cents, 21% are from before 1970.

8
00:00:23,092 --> 00:00:26,199
Before 1960, under 3%.

9
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:29,280
Before 1950, under one.

10
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:33,399
Before 1940, just 26 Cents.

11
00:00:33,479 --> 00:00:34,840
In the words of Martin Lehnen,

12
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:36,600
in his essay "Reflections on Mint

13
00:00:36,679 --> 00:00:39,079
Years": "This data reveals how quickly

14
00:00:39,159 --> 00:00:40,840
scarcity accelerates the further

15
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:42,987
back in time you go."

16
00:00:43,093 --> 00:00:45,359
And of the 1/1 Years: "These CENTS are

17
00:00:45,439 --> 00:00:47,679
extraordinary anomalies with absolute

18
00:00:47,759 --> 00:00:53,640
